  "title": "DataAccessV1dot6",
  "description": "K-05 v1.6, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1196, from T-1190's reads and README open gap 30; DL-391). It only adds to v1.5 (data-access.v1.5.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to v1.4, v1.3, v1.2, v1.1 and v1): every v1.5 definition is here under its own name, the unchanged ones by reference; the changed ones, readOutboxRow.response and readOutboxRow.exchange, take one new optional field, so every v1, v1.1, v1.2, v1.3, v1.4 and v1.5 exchange is a v1.6 exchange. Added: readOutboxRow's answer gives the row's business's sensitive switch, businessSensitive (README item 45; RULES 4.6: under the switch, texts show only the display name; S13-22), read in the same read from K-23 v1's company_kinds of the row's business (pf_switches_a and pf_switches_b; K-26 v1's plugin_switches registry names the switch sensitive: migrations 0019 and 0023): true when any of the business's kinds of work lists it in either flow, false when the business has kinds of work and none lists it, null when it has none or the row has no business, which the caller reads as on (fails closed). A v1.6 call always writes it: readOutboxRow.v1dot6Response is its answer with the switch required. No call, column, grant, index or migration is added. Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
