    "businessSensitive": {
      "title": "BusinessSensitive",
      "description": "The row's business's sensitive switch (README item 45; RULES 4.6: under the switch, texts show only the display name; S13-22). Source: K-23 v1 company_kinds of the row's business (by business_id: company_kinds_business_idx), whose pf_switches_a and pf_switches_b are the plug-in switches turned on in flow A and in flow B, each naming only K-26 v1 plugin_switches entries, in which the switch is sensitive (migrations 0019 and 0023). true: any of the business's kinds of work lists sensitive in either flow; false: the business has kinds of work and none lists it; null: it has none (a sign-up before S1-04 writes them), or the row has no business, for which no kinds of work are read (README default 68). Reason for one value, in either flow: the switch is per kind of work and flow (SPEC-master 5b), and a row about no booking names neither, since no service names its kind of work and the flow its step is read in is the caller's, from the row's bundle (README default 53); so the stricter wins, and a business any of whose kinds of work is sensitive, in any flow, is read as sensitive (README default 66). Null is never off: the caller reads it as on and fails closed (DL-326 note b; DL-391; README default 67). A booking's own switch, through its service's kind of work, is not read (README open gap 30): the caller keeps a row about a booking on. New in v1.6.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ]
    },
    "readOutboxRow.request": {
      "$ref": "data-access.v1.5.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.request"
    },
    "readOutboxRow.response": {
      "title": "ReadOutboxRowResponse",
      "description": "The row as one read of the primary saw it (one read-only transaction, one moment), as v1.3 answers it (README item 35: row, line, recipient, answers, slotSource and openQuestions, each field by reference to v1.3's own definition of it, which v1.4 and v1.5 keep unchanged), with one field more (v1.6, T-1196; README item 45): businessSensitive, the row's business's sensitive switch, true, false or null. It is optional here only so that every v1.3 to v1.5 answer, which has none, is a v1.6 answer and every earlier exchange a v1.6 exchange: a v1.6 call always writes it (readOutboxRow.v1dot6Response), and a consumer reads an answer without it as null, which is on, never off (README default 67). Never a sealed value, the inbound words, the recipient's address, a key or a wrapping key's name (rule 7); and of the business's kinds of work only the switch's one value, never a kind of work, its facts, its trade name or another switch (README default 69).",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "result": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/result"
        },
        "outboxRowId": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/outboxRowId"
        },
        "businessId": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/businessId"
        },
        "readAt": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/readAt"
        },
        "row": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/row"
        },
        "line": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/line"
        },
        "recipient": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/recipient"
        },
        "answers": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/answers"
        },
        "slotSource": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/slotSource"
        },
        "businessSensitive": {
          "description": "The row's business's sensitive switch (businessSensitive; README item 45), which fills SlotSource.sensitive for a row about no booking: null and a missing field are on, never off, and a row about a booking stays on (README item 35's table, row source). New in v1.6.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/businessSensitive"
        },
        "openQuestions": {
          "$ref": "data-access.v1.3.schema.json#/$defs/readOutboxRow.response/properties/openQuestions"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "result",
        "outboxRowId",
        "businessId",
        "readAt",
        "row",
        "line",
        "recipient",
        "answers",
        "slotSource",
        "openQuestions"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "readOutboxRow.v1dot6Response": {
      "title": "ReadOutboxRowV1dot6Response",
      "description": "readOutboxRow's answer as a v1.6 call writes it (README item 45): every field of readOutboxRow.response, by reference, with businessSensitive always stated, true, false or null, never left out. readOutboxRow.response takes it as optional only so that v1.3 to v1.5's answers stay valid; this is the definition a v1.6 producer's answers are checked against (db/repo's readOutboxRow, T-1197), so no consumer meets a v1.6 answer that leaves the switch out and could take it as off (refuse-outbox-row-switch-left-out). New in v1.6.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
